<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $2.7 bln in Oct 28 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $2.7 bln in Oct 28 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $2.7 billion in the October 28 week to $3,781.4 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $1.5 billion to $4,814.7 billion. M-1 rose $2.5 billion to $1,081.3 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,774.1 billion versus $3,768.2 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
